w(f"1. **In FishLab's arbiter**, with KRAKEN played exactly as its own integration guide requires, KRAKEN loses: **{d['sets_margin_A']:+.3f}** {ci(*d['sets_margin_ci'])} sets per game and "
  f"**{pct(d['winA'])}** {ci(*d['winA_ci'], f='{:.1%}')} of games over {d['games']:,} games under FishLab's rules"
  + (f", and {nn['sets_margin_A']:+.3f} {ci(*nn['sets_margin_ci'])} sets per game over {nn['games']:,} games under KRAKEN's own declare-on-turn dialect." if nn else "."))
w(f"2. **In KV's own arbiter** (their Python engine, their rules, their bridge revision 2, fresh seeds) the paper's number reproduces: **{kv['margin']:+.3f}** {ci(*kv['ci'])} over {kv['games']:,} games, with SESTINA declaring correctly only {pct(kv['sestina_decl_acc'])} of the time.")
w(f"3. **The difference is a defect in their bridge into SESTINA**, `fish4/dylan_v07.py`: it resets SESTINA with its *current* hand as if that were the hand it was dealt, then replays the whole public history on top. "
  f"Correcting that one line — passing the hand as dealt, which is what FishLab's own driver passes — and re-playing the identical deals in their arbiter moves the result by **{dh['paired_vs_rev2'][0]:+.3f}** {ci(dh['paired_vs_rev2'][1], dh['paired_vs_rev2'][2])} sets per game (paired, {dh['paired_vs_rev2'][3]:,} games). "
  f"Under the corrected bridge KRAKEN loses in their arbiter too: **{dh['margin']:+.3f}** {ci(*dh['ci'])} sets per game, {pct(dh['kv_win'])} of games"
  + (f"; on {big['games']:,} further fresh games, {big['margin']:+.3f} {ci(*big['ci'])}." if big else "."))
w(f"4. The two arbiters then agree. SESTINA's declaration accuracy in their arbiter rises from {pct(kv['sestina_decl_acc'])} to {pct(dh['sestina_decl_acc'])}, "
  f"which is what it measures at natively ({pct(d['declB'])} in FishLab); the '{pct(mega['declare_right_dylan'])}' the paper builds its mechanism story on is the bridge, not the engine.")
w("")
if lad:
    w(f"The forced-endgame bridge repair the paper describes (their revision 2) is real but immaterial at this scale: giving the mover FishLab's full willingness ladder moves the margin by {lad['paired_vs_rev2'][0]:+.3f} {ci(lad['paired_vs_rev2'][1], lad['paired_vs_rev2'][2])}.")
    w("")
w("## 1. What was tested, and what was held fixed")
w("")
w("| item | value |")
w("|---|---|")
w(f"| KRAKEN | the vendored package at `engine/external/kraken` (KRAKEN v1.0: `V06_DEPLOYED` + `claim_forced_exhaustive=1`). The upstream branch head `5da2040` (2026-09-01, KRAKEN v1.1) was fetched and run on the same seed: **bit-identical** ({pct(up['winRateA'])} vs {pct(vend['winRateA'])} win rate, {up['meanSetsA']:.3f}/{up['meanSetsB']:.3f} vs {vend['meanSetsA']:.3f}/{vend['meanSetsB']:.3f} sets, {up['nAsksA']}/{vend['nAsksA']} asks, {up['nDeclA']}/{vend['nDeclA']} declarations). The v1.1 paper says its deployed configuration is unchanged from v1.0; this confirms it. |")
w("| SESTINA | the frozen spec from `engine/fishbot_v07.json` (`v07:r12=25,...,maxq=26`; its `allparamsSpec` form is what KV's bridge sends and equals `external_v07/v07_spec.txt` in their repository). The paper pins FishLab commit `d017fbc`; between that commit and the build used here (`f9b4743` plus uncommitted work) the only changes under `engine/src/` to files the policy depends on are two additive hooks (`Agent::observeResolution`, and the `kraken`/`bot:` factory branches). |")
w("| KRAKEN inside FishLab | `engine/src/kv6.hpp`, which follows the three requirements of `kraken/README.md`: every seat is polled off-turn through their proof-only channel, cards travel as names with the half-suit permutation derived from their own `{\"op\":\"cards\"}` table, and any error, illegal move or dead process aborts the run rather than substituting a move. A wrong declaration additionally hands KRAKEN the true holders, as its own engine reveals them. No timeouts. Zero bridge faults in every run below. |")
w("| SESTINA inside KV's arbiter | their own `fish4/dylan_v07.py` (bridge revision 2; the upstream file is byte-identical to the vendored one) driving their own `external_v07/shim_decide.cpp`, compiled here against this repository's `engine/src`; run by a driver that reproduces `scripts4/mega_match.py`'s design (`V06_DEPLOYED` vs `dylan_v07`, `wrong_distribution_outcome=\"opponent\"`, each deal played from both parities). Zero fallbacks, zero unfinished games. |")
w("| machine | one Apple M5 Pro, 15 cores, several batteries sharing it. |")
w("")
